2. Tight coupling and loose coupling and what IOC does?
Tight coupling: two classes highly dependent with each other, for example, we create an instance of
a class inside another class, so the instance is tightly coupling with this class
Loose coupling: minimal dependency, more flexible, which is a good practice
IOC uses loose coupling, instead creating objects manually, spring boot IOC container manage beans for us, so
dependencies are loose coupling, which is more flexible for scaling and introducing new features

3. What is MVC pattern?
M: model, container of data
View: front-end view
Controller: handle requests
The center of MVC is dispatcherServlet. Front-controller map front-end requests to controller, return result to
dispatcherServlet, then dispatcherServlet call controller to handle requests. The controller will call services,
repositories, database and return view and model. dispatcherServlet call view solver and insert the data into
new. Finally, dispatcherServlet return html back to browser.

